Swords kill the body; wit destroys

Fame, family, and regal joys.

374 THE PANCHATANTRA

"Thus, success comes with minimum effort to a man of wisdom and manliness. For

Wisdom broods o'er the inception;

Memory does not fail; Means appear to predilection;

Counsels wise prevail; Sparkles fruitful meditation;

Mind attains its height; Joy achieves its consummation
